.TH SYSTEMD-PILOT 1 "October 2026" "systemd Pilot 4.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
systemd-pilot \- manage systemd services locally and over SSH
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B systemd-pilot
[\fIOPTION\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B systemd-pilot
is a graphical front end for
.BR systemctl (1).
It lists the system and user services of this computer, or of remote
machines reached over SSH, and can start, stop, restart, enable and
disable them, show their status, logs, unit file and properties, and
create new services.
.PP
Changes to system services on this computer are authorized through
polkit
.RB ( pkexec (1)).
On remote machines they use
.BR sudo (8);
the password is sent on standard input and kept only for the current
connection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print debug messages.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the available options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd\-pilot/hosts.json
Saved remote hosts. Their passwords are kept in the keyring.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd\-pilot/known_hosts
Host keys accepted in systemd Pilot, in addition to
.IR ~/.ssh/known_hosts .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR systemd.unit (5)
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/mfat/systemd-pilot/issues
